      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Both strategies are effective, but they work differently: scarcity pricing directly manipulates value perception, while a countdown timer manipulates perceived urgency through social proof. Given the sudden traffic surge, a countdown timer might be safer to avoid alienating customers who feel tricked, whereas pricing changes could stall future sales if the \"price jump\" feels unjustified. You should probably test a limited-time discount (a soft scarcity model) rather than a hard price hike to convert this traffic without damaging long-term trust.",
